    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a preliminary risk assessment model for some new urban reinsurance products in the mid-Atlantic region. We're looking at some areas that have seen pretty rapid demographic shifts and an influx of new resident groups over the last 24 months. When you're building out community-level volatility profiles, what kind of socio-demographic indicators do you usually prioritize to account for potential instability or shifts in local economic patterns?",
